EXT. SINKING FISHING TRAWLER, BERING SEA - NIGHT

Black swells. A bow rising and falling, deck awash. Two survivors cling to the wheelhouse roof.

CAPTAIN WINIFRED OYELOWO-STRAND (50s, orange survival suit, a split lip) and DECKHAND AMADEO TRUJILLO-BELL (20s, no gloves, teeth chattering).

AMADEO
Captain, the lifeboat's gone!

WINIFRED
I know!

AMADEO
We'll freeze!

WINIFRED
We won't freeze. We'll drown first. It's quicker.

AMADEO
That's not funny!

WINIFRED
I wasn't joking.

AMADEO
(laughs, then sobs)
I'm twenty-two.

WINIFRED
I'm fifty-four. I've done this three times.

AMADEO
Done what?

WINIFRED
Sunk.

AMADEO
How do you...

WINIFRED
You hold on. That's the whole trick. Hold on till the boat stops being your problem.

AMADEO
What if it never does?

WINIFRED
Then you hold on to me.

A swell slams the hull. Spray. They scream. The boat tilts, groans, and settles.

AMADEO
Captain!

WINIFRED
Still here!

AMADEO
Still here!

WINIFRED
Then the rest is arithmetic.
